---
import { BACKER_PRIVACY_PATH, REFUND_DAYS, TERMS_PATH } from "../../../lib/gloss/campaign";

/**
 * How backing works, in the same words as section 6 of the Gloss terms.
 * Change the two together: backers rely on this promise.
 */
const rules = [
  { title: "You pay when you back.", body: "Stripe takes the payment. We never see your card." },
  { title: "Each language has its own goal and closing date.", body: "Your money goes only to the language you chose." },
  { title: "If it misses its goal, you get it all back.", body: `We refund every payment for that language within ${REFUND_DAYS} days of its closing date.` },
  { title: "Changed your mind?", body: "Until your language reaches its goal, email us and we refund you in full." },
  { title: "We show where the money went.", body: "Every backer gets a report of what we spent it on." },
];
---

<div>
  <ol class="space-y-4">
    {rules.map((rule) => (
      <li class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-white/[0.06] bg-white dark:bg-white/[0.03] p-5">
        <p class="font-semibold text-text">{rule.title}</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 mt-1">{rule.body}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-4">
    The full rules are in section 6 of the <a href={TERMS_PATH} class="text-[var(--gloss-sage)] hover:underline">Gloss terms</a>.
    What we keep about backers: <a href={BACKER_PRIVACY_PATH} class="text-[var(--gloss-sage)] hover:underline">backer privacy notice</a>.
  </p>
</div>
